-- title:
--   Chart points of the special fibre give rational affine places
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q\nmid N_0$, and an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $q$ together with a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{to}\kappa$ from the Igusa base ring $\mathrm{DRLevel.R}\ q$ to $\kappa$. Let $M$ be a `CurveModel` for $\kappa$ and the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ \kappa\ N_0 = \kappa(j_{q}, j_{q}^{(N_0)}) \subseteq \kappa((q))$ generated by the Laurent series $\mathrm{jqModC}\ \kappa$ and its $N_0$-fold $q$-expansion: thus an integral scheme $M.C$, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\kappa$, with an isomorphism $M.\mathrm{ffEquiv}$ of that field with the function field of $M.C$ over $\kappa$, and a bijection $M.\mathrm{placeOfPoint}$ from closed points of $M.C$ to places of the field over $\kappa$ matching stalks with valuation subrings. Let $e : M.C \to \mathrm{fibre0}\ \mathrm{to}\kappa = X_0(N_0)_{\mathrm{Igusa}} \times_{\mathrm{Spec}\,\mathrm{R}\,q} \mathrm{Spec}\,\kappa$ be an isomorphism over $\mathrm{Spec}\,\kappa$, i.e. $e$ followed by the second projection is $M.\mathrm{toBase}$. Write $U$ for the preimage under $e$ followed by the first projection of the open image of the $j$-finite chart $\mathrm{\iota Fin}\ N_0\ q$, assumed non-empty. Assume the chart pin: for every $b$ in the chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\ N_0\ q$, letting $\mathrm{read}b$ be the element of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ \kappa\ N_0$ obtained by pulling $b$ back to a section over $U$, taking its germ at the generic point and applying $M.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, one has $\mathrm{read}b = \mathrm{jGeomGen}\ \kappa\ N_0$ whenever $b = \mathrm{jChartFin}\ N_0\ q$, and $\mathrm{read}b = \mathrm{jNGeomGen}\ \kappa\ N_0$ whenever $b$, viewed as a Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$, equals $\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb{Q}\ N_0\ \mathrm{jq}$. Finally let $pt : \mathrm{Spec}\,\kappa \to \mathrm{fibre0}\ \mathrm{to}\kappa$ be a section of the second projection whose composite with the first projection factors as $\mathrm{Spec}$ of a ring homomorphism $\psi : \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\ N_0\ q \to \kappa$ followed by $\mathrm{\iota Fin}\ N_0\ q$. The conclusion is that the image of the closed point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,\kappa$ under $pt$ and then $e^{-1}$ is a closed point of $M.C$, and that the associated place $P = M.\mathrm{placeOfPoint}$ of that point satisfies: $\kappa$ surjects onto the residue field of $P$; both $\mathrm{jGeomGen}\ \kappa\ N_0$ and $\mathrm{jNGeomGen}\ \kappa\ N_0$ lie in the valuation subring of $P$ (the predicate $\mathrm{IsAffineGeomPlace}\ \kappa\ N_0$); and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\ \kappa\ N_0) = \psi(\mathrm{jChartFin}\ N_0\ q)$.
--
--   This is the point-to-place half of the dictionary for the characteristic-$q$ fibre of the Igusa-style model of $X_0(N_0)$: a $\kappa$-point lying in the $j$-finite chart yields a rational place of the modular function field at which $j$ and its $N_0$-fold $q$-expansion are regular, and the value of $j$ there is the chart coordinate's value $\psi(j)$. It feeds [`ModularCurve.DRLevel.exists_nodeEquiv_placeOfPoint_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRLevel.exists_nodeEquiv_placeOfPoint_eq), where supersingularity of a place is reduced to a condition on this $j$-value.
